## Audit conclusion

Phase 1.5 remains **in progress**. Repository implementation and closure hardening are present, but the master completion gate requires tree-content-bound publication evidence and real external evidence that code and fixtures cannot manufacture.

`npm run phase15:audit:local` reports only `localReady`. `npm run ci:prepublish` produces `publicationReady` for the exact candidate. `npm run phase15:audit` intentionally exits nonzero until `localReady`, `publicationReady`, and `externalReady` are all true. The closure sentence is emitted only by the latter command.

`localReady` never authorizes publication. `publicationReady` never claims GitHub/provider/deployment evidence. Per ADR-0018, evidence is bound to the candidate's git tree content hash, not its commit SHA — a real GitHub merge always produces a new commit SHA, so commit-SHA equality could never survive a real merge; a changed tree still invalidates evidence, but a merge-generated SHA change alone does not. The `.github/workflows/pr-prepublish.yml` workflow now runs `ci:prepublish` on the pull request itself as a real pre-merge CI job (job id `prepublish`); adding that check context to the branch-protection ruleset and enabling "require branches up to date before merging" remains explicit follow-up work, not yet done.

## Increment status

| Increment | Repository state | Evidence state |
|---|---|---|
| M1 — contracts and governance | Implemented | Eight roles and source hashes validate |
| PR-A — telemetry foundation | Implemented | Schema, redaction, normalization, sink, and failure tests pass |
| PR-B — context preflight/compiler | Implemented | Determinism, reference-first, deduplication, exact-data, budget, and conditional-auditor tests pass |
| PR-C — eval harness | Implemented | Sixteen required fixture families validate; deterministic baseline is explicitly not tuning-eligible |
| PR-D — tool policy gateway | Implemented | Role/path/action allow-ask-deny and bypass tests pass; Claude PreToolUse hook is configured |
| PR-E — provider vertical slice | Implemented and exercised | Claude, OpenAI, and Codex CLI adapter contracts pass; real subscription-authenticated Codex evidence closes the representative and repeated-baseline gates |
| PR-F — risk/council engine | Implemented | Risk 0–3, independence, cross-provider, stale-diff, blocker, and adjudication tests pass |
| PR-G — tuning gate | Implemented and baselined | Two distinct risk-0 scenarios have three real Codex repetitions each; the accepted bounded aggregate applies no tuning and claims neither Claude review nor unmeasured cost |
| PR-H — publication gate | Implemented and hardened | Manifest-owned PR metadata, shared local/GitHub policy, tree-content-bound prepublication evidence (ADR-0018), a real pre-merge `prepublish` CI check, readback verification, and deterministic denial are covered |
| PR-I — release/provenance | Implemented and exercised through staging | Exact-candidate attestation and staging promotion/verification pass; production and rollback remain blocked |
| PR-J — completion audit/freeze | Audit implemented | Freeze remains blocked by the three external gates below |

## External observation

The refreshed read-only GitHub observation on August 9, 2026 found a public repository and an active `Protect main` ruleset with pull requests, resolved conversations, signed commits, CodeQL, deletion/non-fast-forward protection, no bypass actors, and the required `Agent platform / contracts-policy-evals` job. Closure-hardening PR #32 passed every required check and merged as `7dc157d2f84670145c4f1b5fcba274cf06f6f4dc`.

Preview, staging, and production environments exist. Production has a custom branch policy and administrator bypass is disabled, but it has no required reviewer. The `agent-evals` environment does not exist. These facts are recorded without secrets in `agent-platform/baselines/external-controls-observation-2026-08-09.json`.

The representative Codex evidence remains preserved in `agent-platform/baselines/live-codex-representative-2026-08-09.json`. A separate accepted aggregate in `agent-platform/baselines/live-codex-multiscenario-2026-08-09.json` binds six successful ChatGPT-authenticated Codex CLI runs to candidate `e27ddcb7026059b48c5e97277c6e9d386511b8a5`: `bounded-typescript-bug` and `documentation-only-change`, each repeated three times with distinct WorkUnit, AgentRun, ProviderRun, and EvalResult correlations. Task success and evidence completeness are 1.0 with zero tool calls, retries, security failures, or scope violations. Prompts, responses, credentials, provider metadata, unmeasured cost, and unperformed independent provider review are not claimed; no tuning was applied. These risk-0 evals do not require cross-provider council evidence, and no Claude run is claimed.

The exact merge candidate was built and attested in PR-quality run `31342391343`. Independent `gh attestation verify` enforcement bound `beacon-dist.tar.gz` digest `f4ff3b08a96f2e89640710771f263e6a60ab0dfae43d62b6a56b7e415be9d7ed` to `.github/workflows/pr-quality.yml`, `refs/heads/main`, and the merge SHA. Staging run `31342520379` verified and promoted that same artifact as Worker version `3e4de117-f432-4a3a-b3fd-aecedf295c9f`; post-deploy run `31342578773` then passed the live status and security-header checks. The bounded promotion and verification records are artifacts `9046260894` and `9046271178`.

## Failed hard gates

- real production promotion and post-deploy verification;
- real known-good rollback drill.

Non-bypassable external production approval is now closed. Production administrator bypass is disabled, and the environment has one required reviewer (self-review not prevented). A separate, previously-undocumented bypass path was found and closed the same day: the Cloudflare native Git integration for the `beaconco9` Worker auto-deployed independent of this GitHub environment gate. It was manually disconnected and the disconnect was empirically verified — merging a trivial change to `main` produced zero Workers Builds check-runs and no change to the live production `etag`. Production dispatch and rollback remain prohibited until the two gates above have real evidence.

## Freeze rule

Do not change this page, the roadmap, or the phase status to complete/frozen until `npm run phase15:audit` passes using real reviewed evidence. Workflow definitions, synthetic adapter responses, deterministic fixtures, and unverified external settings do not satisfy live gates.
